WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.534
-Thank you so much.
It's so wonderful to be here.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:04.767
-We love having you here.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.000
But we have some
very exciting news.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.300
You're expecting.
-I am.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.367
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.667
-That's the best news
in the world.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:11.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.000
-This is the third baby.
-Yeah.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.467
-Third baby --

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.000
-And I think the last.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
-[ Laughs ] Really?
You feeling it? Yeah.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.033
-This one was a surprise.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.067
-Okay.
-Yes.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:27.267
No, this pregnancy happened
to me.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.467
Yes.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.067
[ Laughter ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.434
But -- Uh-huh.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.901
Um, but we're thrilled.
-That's funny. Yeah.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:37.033
You have two boys already.
-Two boys. Yeah.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.968
-Cyrus is 10, and Rowan is 4.
-10 and 4.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.133
So, it's going to be
quite a big span there.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.334
But, yeah.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.000
-How are they feeling
about this?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.167
-Cyrus was sort of resigned
to it.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:52.067
I mean, the worst
has already happened.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.701
His name is Rowan.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:56.767
[ Laughter ]
And yeah.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.534
But Rowan has more to lose.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:00:59.701
Like, he has more at stake.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:05.334
And he was categorically
opposed to the idea.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.701
He said, "Yeah, no, no.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.033
I don't like it.
I don't like it.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.634
I like -- I like peace, Mama."

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.033
I was like, "You like peace?"

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.367
-"I like peace" is what he said?

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:17.234
-That's rich, because that dude
does not shut up.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.701
[ Laughter ]
-You like peace?

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.200
That's so funny.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.567
-No, he said, "When it comes
out of your tummy,

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.634
we'll give it to a family
that doesn't have a baby."

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.167
[ Audience laughs, "awws" ]
-That's a good plan.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.167
-'Cause we're done.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.834
-He has a good plan.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.100
He's like, "I'm the baby, man.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.434
I can't be a new baby."

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.701
-So, no, he was
less than thrilled.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:38.067
But then we talked about
how when the baby comes out,

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:41.067
it's going to be pretty dumb,
doesn't know a lot.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.801
-Yeah.
-So, you know,

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.234
it's going to need assistance
and some educating.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.634
He kind of --
That was interesting to him.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:50.701
He liked the idea of being a
sort of condescending presence.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.467
So, now he's a little --
a little more optimistic.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:58.367
-You know, every time
that you've been pregnant,

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.834
you've been on our show.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.100
-Okay.
-So, this is --

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.901
-Yeah, no, no, it makes me feel
like I've always been pregnant.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.267
-No, I meant to say,
it's good luck.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.267
-Yeah, sure.
-And your kids --

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.767
everyone's been --
your whole family's been --

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.801
-It makes me afraid
to be booked, basically.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.434
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.267
-That's interesting, yeah.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.267
But the whole family's
been on our show.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.701
-Yeah.
-That's interesting.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.167
-Yes, that's true.
-Yeah, it's a family affair.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.934
-The whole brood.
That's right.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.067
-I want to talk about
"Fleishman Is In Trouble."

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.968
Man, you've been getting
great reviews for this.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:31.067
Congratulations.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.634
You got nominated
for a Golden Globe.

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:35.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Critic's Choice Award.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.200
Not too shabby.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.868
The series is based
on a best-selling novel.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.601
How did you hear about the book?

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:44.300
-Actually, my best friend
not only gave it to me,

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.901
she dragged me to the nearest
bookstore, bought it for me,

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.133
shoved it in my bag, and said,
"You have to read this book

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.667
'cause I need to talk to you
about the ending."

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:52.801
Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:56.000
And actually,
I was going to do reshoots

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.868
on another limited series I did
called "The Essex Serpent,"

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.167
which took place
in the Victorian era.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.334
And that was in my set bag

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:05.934
because I, like, you know,
had this assignment

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.234
from my bestie.
-Yeah, you had to read the book.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.167
-Yeah, so I was, like,
in a corset

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:12.100
and surrounded
by this Victorian environment.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.901
-We have a photo.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.234
-We have a photo
of you reading the book.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.334
-And I was reading the book.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.100
And, you know --
-Here's you on set.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:23.934
-And then I got the offer that
week to play Rachel Fleishman.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.033
I know. Isn't that weird?

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.434
So, yeah.

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:27.767
-So you're reading it here,

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:30.000
and then you get the offer
to be the person

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.501
in this book you're reading.
-Yeah!

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:33.067
-That's magic.
-Isn't that funny?

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's magic!

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.667
-I know. I know.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:36.834
-It's a fantastic book.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.434
-Oh, it is. It's great.
It's great.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:41.968
And I did finally
get to the end, and yeah.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.234
-Yeah.
-And so --

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.100
Taffy is talented.
-She's wonderful.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.834
She's a dear friend
and she's very gifted,

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.601
and, yeah, she wrote
a great character

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.234
that I was very fortunate
to play.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.501
-But you and Jesse Eisenberg
play a married couple

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.133
going through a divorce.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.601
-A hard time, yeah.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.467
-He was on the show
pretty recently.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:01.534
And was telling me a story that
he met you years ago at a party

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.100
and thought
that he found his soulmate.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.434
-Uh-huh.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.133
-And told his now wife,

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.567
but it was his girlfriend
who was at the party with him,

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.767
which is hilarious.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.300
I think he said
he was stoned or something.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.200
And he went up to you,
and he's like,

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.100
"I think I just found someone,
my soulmate."

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.234
And she goes, "That's
Claire Danes. Good luck."

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.767
She actually said that
to him, yeah.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.868
Do you remember
this meeting at all?

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:25.501
-I did not remember
the meeting.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.601
Yeah. No.
He told me that.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.300
There was a cast dinner,
and he said,

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.300
do you remember meeting --
No.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.367
But -- But I love Jesse
very much

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.534
and was thrilled that he found

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:43.167
such a strong connection
in our introduction.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.634
But no.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:47.234
I really did have the dreamiest
time divorcing him.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.601
He's wonderful.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.667
I did. I know.
-That's a great way to put it.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.534
You guys -- What goes behind
when you're doing a role

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.033
where you have to get divorced?

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.701
-Well, we didn't have
that much time to rehearse,

00:04:57.701 --> 00:05:01.767
so it was fairly dense
and sort of accelerated.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.467
But our directors, John and Val,

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:07.868
who ironically are
a very happily married couple,

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.534
put together
some exercises for us.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.634
So, we did some
journaling together.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:16.434
We sat in our respective
bean bags, curiously.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.734
That seemed important.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:21.534
And we were given prompts,
we were asked questions,

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.300
and we had, like,
two minutes to answer them.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.467
And then we read them
to each other --

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.234
like, what initially
attracted us to each other,

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.400
why we're disappointed
in each other now.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.234
Just mildly uncomfortable,
but also very annoying,

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:38.467
because he's a very gifted
professional writer as well.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.100
-Jesse, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.834
So, wrote these very articulate,

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:48.200
kind of poetic musings
about our characters' history.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.801
And I just had words
to offer up.

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:52.534
-You're like, "Hey, Jesse,
dial it down a little bit.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.167
Come on,
this isn't the part here."

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:55.167
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.767
So, he won that game.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:06:01.467
But then we played dodgeball
too, which was surprising.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:02.868
-Really?
-And I did not wear

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.467
the right footwear.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:05.801
-Did you know you were
playing Dodgeball?

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:07.100
-No! Nobody said that.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.167
-When was the last time
you played dodgeball?

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.167
-Fifth grade.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.501
-Yeah, probably, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.868
I was wearing clogs,
which I don't recommend.

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:16.267
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.234
-But I think I did win that one.

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:20.234
-Ooh!

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.767
There's one scene
that went viral.

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.701
Your character's
at a yoga retreat,

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.801
and you're asked to do
a primal scream.

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:29.801
-Yeah.

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:31.367
-And man, oh, man, Claire Danes,

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:32.534
you went for it, bud.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.067
You went for it.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:37.234
And it went viral all over
the Internet the next day.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:43.234
How did you pull off the scream?

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:48.467
-Well, I'm not, like,
formally trained.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:51.634
I work in the television,
not the theater.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:52.901
-Uh-huh.

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:55.234
-So I was worried that I was
gonna blow my voice out.

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:58.267
But John and Val
were aware of the risk.

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:02.000
And so, yeah, we ended up
doing one take.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.200
But I was kind of surprised
that I had all that breath.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.000
It just kept...going,
the scream.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.501
After a while,
I was just sort of observing it.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.567
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:12.934
-I felt like
I was riding this wave.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:14.934
-It must feel good to just
do that and just get it out.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:19.033
-It was great. I recommend it.
-Yeah.

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:21.767
-For anyone who hasn't seen
the series yet,

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:24.434
how do you explain
what it's about?

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:27.133
-It's about a New York
middle-aged couple

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.801
who are going through a divorce.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:34.601
The story's told
by the husband's,

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:37.667
kind of, college-aged friend.

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:40.534
And it broadens out,
and suddenly,

00:07:40.534 --> 00:07:42.133
there are many
middle-aged New Yorkers

00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:44.834
going through various
crises of their own.

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:46.968
-It's fantastic.
I want to show a clip.

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:49.434
Here's Claire Danes
in "Fleishman Is In Trouble."

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:50.734
Take a look at this.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:54.534
-I-I haven't been
drinking coffee, so --

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:55.701
-What is going on?

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:56.968
-God, there are so many
parts to this.

00:07:56.968 --> 00:07:58.868
-Rachel.

00:07:58.868 --> 00:08:01.067
-I-I also have all this tea.

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:02.567
It might be easier.

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:04.901
I, um, I bought all this tea

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:06.501
'cause I was having
a hard time sleeping.

00:08:06.501 --> 00:08:09.567
But all it did was just keep me
in the bathroom all night.

00:08:09.567 --> 00:08:12.434
I feel like I-I don't know
where my toaster is,

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:15.701
but -- but I do have some bread.

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:17.300
-Rachel.

00:08:20.901 --> 00:08:22.601
-[ Crying ]
I want to be honest with you.

00:08:25.634 --> 00:08:30.901
I don't think I-I can
make you coffee right now.

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:33.801
-Oh, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:35.801
Claire Danes,
you're unbelievable.

00:08:35.801 --> 00:08:38.167
The FX series
"Fleishman Is In Trouble"

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:40.334
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:08:40.334 --> 00:08:41.734
Roman Reigns joins us next.

00:08:41.734 --> 00:08:42.801
Stick around, everybody.

